def author(c,s,m,a):
 c('b228','纜索承載、雙船廂獨立性與高架航道銜接~Cable load sharing, independent caissons and elevated-reach interfaces',['wallonia-lift','sofico-lift','canal-lift'],r'''
船廂水位與額外質量~Caisson level and extra mass||浮船排水只在船廂水位固定時保持總質量，水位偏差則直接增加或減少水量。大平面船廂即使小幅水位變化，也會使配重平衡出現明顯差異。~Vessel displacement preserves total mass only at a fixed caisson level. A level error directly changes water volume, so even a small change across a large plan area noticeably alters counterweight balance.||取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³。假設船廂有效面積1200 m²、水位偏高0.03 m，額外淡水質量ρAΔh=36000 kg=36 t；忽略船體水線面排除面積。~Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³. Assume effective caisson area 1200 m² and excess level 0.03 m. Added freshwater mass ρAΔh=36000 kg=36 t, neglecting the vessel waterplane exclusion.||比較入廂前後多點水位並平均波動，核對面積是否已扣除船體水線面；另以索力總和反算質量，檢查水位推估和力學量測是否一致。~Average multiple level readings around entry, checking whether vessel waterplane area is excluded. Independently infer mass from summed tensions and compare the level-based and force-based estimates.||若船舶長時間遮蔽部分水面，沿用全空廂面積會高估增量。水位計基準偏差又會使每次循環都出現同方向失配，不能誤判為索具永久伸長。~Using empty-caisson area while a vessel occupies the surface overstates the increment. Gauge datum bias creates same-direction mismatch each cycle and must not be mistaken for permanent rope extension.||浮船船廂總重在任何水位變化下都完全不變。~A floating-vessel caisson keeps identical total mass despite any water-level change.
纜索群載重分配~Cable-group load sharing||多條懸吊索讓總荷載分散，但單索張力取決於長度、剛度與均衡裝置。總索數除重量只提供理想平均，不保證最大索力或端部連接需求。~Many suspension ropes distribute total load, but individual tension depends on length, stiffness and equalization. Dividing weight by rope count gives an ideal mean rather than the maximum tension or anchorage demand.||假設懸吊合力64 MN、80條索理想均分，每索0.8 MN；若一組10條承擔總力20%，該組每索1.28 MN。~Assume suspension resultant 64 MN shared ideally by eighty ropes, giving 0.8 MN each. If ten ropes carry twenty percent of total force, each in that group carries 1.28 MN.||建立全部索力分布並比較同組與跨組差異，用總和核對懸吊平衡；將長度校準、端接移動和均衡梁位置一起記錄，查異常能否重複。~Map all tensions within and between groups and check their sum against suspended load. Record length calibration, anchorage movement and equalizer position, testing whether anomalies repeat under matched conditions.||索力平均值正常仍可能藏有少數高載索，替換索的剛度差亦會重新分配荷載。若只抽測外側容易接近的索，會忽略內部群組的系統性偏差。~A normal mean can conceal a few overloaded ropes, and replacement-rope stiffness changes sharing. Sampling only easily reached outer ropes can miss a systematic imbalance in internal groups.||總重量除索數就能代表任何一條索的實際最大張力。~Total weight divided by rope count gives every ropes actual maximum tension.
均衡梁槓桿關係~Equalizer lever equilibrium||均衡梁藉槓桿轉動重新分配索力，但臂長、接頭摩擦與行程限制會影響效果。能轉動的機構不一定仍處於有效均衡範圍。~An equalizer redistributes tension through lever rotation, with arm length, joint friction and travel limits controlling performance. A movable mechanism is not necessarily still within its effective equalization range.||假設總力2 MN、兩臂長0.8與1.2 m，力矩平衡T1×0.8=T2×1.2，T1=1.2 MN、T2=0.8 MN；理想無摩擦鉸接。~Assume total force 2 MN and lever arms 0.8 and 1.2 m. From T1×0.8=T2×1.2, T1=1.2 MN and T2=0.8 MN, for an ideal frictionless pivot.||同時量測梁角、兩端位移和張力，檢查是否滿足力矩平衡；在載重反向變化時比較遲滯，並確認梁端尚未碰觸幾何行程限制。~Measure beam angle, end movement and tension together and check moment equilibrium. Compare hysteresis during opposite load changes and verify that ends have not reached geometric travel stops.||軸銷摩擦可讓張力差暫時維持而梁不轉，接近止擋時均衡功能也會退化。只確認梁體沒有裂紋，無法證明整個調平機構仍能有效動作。~Pin friction can preserve unequal tension without movement, and approaching a stop degrades equalization. An uncracked beam alone does not establish that the complete leveling mechanism still functions effectively.||均衡梁存在就表示兩端張力必定完全相等。~The presence of an equalizer means both end tensions are always equal.
索輪曲率與彎曲循環~Sheave curvature and bending cycles||鋼索反覆繞過輪槽時，單絲承受彎曲與接觸作用，輪徑對索徑比是重要幾何指標。該比值不能單獨給出疲勞壽命，還需張力譜和索結構。~Ropes repeatedly bending over grooves experience wire bending and contact. Sheave-to-rope diameter ratio is useful geometry, but fatigue life also depends on tension spectrum and rope construction.||假設索輪直徑4 m、鋼索直徑0.08 m，D/d=50；若一年20000次繞曲，5年為100000次，僅計數而非壽命保證。~Assume sheave diameter 4 m and rope diameter 0.08 m, giving D/d=50. At 20000 bends annually, five years gives 100000 bends, a count rather than a life guarantee.||對照輪槽尺寸、索徑和彎曲循環紀錄，檢查斷絲位置是否集中於反覆繞曲區；把潤滑狀態、磁漏檢測與外觀證據合併判讀。~Compare groove geometry, rope diameter and bending records, locating broken wires relative to repeated bend zones. Interpret lubrication, magnetic inspection and visual evidence together rather than using any one indicator alone.||索輪磨耗可改變接觸壓力而不改變名義輪徑，內部斷絲也未必外露。若只用循環次數或直徑比決定狀況，會漏掉局部磨擦與腐蝕。~Groove wear changes contact pressure without changing nominal diameter, and internal wire breaks may be hidden. Cycle count or diameter ratio alone misses localized rubbing and corrosion mechanisms.||索輪直徑比足夠大就能保證鋼索不會發生疲勞。~A sufficiently large sheave-diameter ratio guarantees that ropes cannot fatigue.
捲揚轉速與機械效率~Winch speed and mechanical efficiency||捲揚機把索的線速度轉為轉速，減速機改變轉矩和速度但不創造功率。有效鼓徑隨繞層可能改變，因此編碼器轉角不一定固定對應索長。~Winches convert rope speed to rotation. Gear reduction exchanges speed and torque without creating power, while changing winding radius can alter the relationship between encoder angle and rope travel.||假設有效鼓半徑1.5 m、索速0.15 m/s，轉速n=60v/(2πr)=0.9549 rpm；單層固定半徑，未含滑移。~Assume effective drum radius 1.5 m and rope speed 0.15 m/s. n=60v/(2πr)=0.9549 rpm, for a fixed single-layer radius without slip.||比較編碼器轉角與獨立索長量測，按繞層和鼓槽位置分組；再核對輸入轉速、輸出轉矩與功率，確認效率不超過物理上限。~Compare encoder angle with independent rope travel, grouped by winding layer and groove position. Check input speed, output torque and power together to ensure inferred efficiency respects physical limits.||多層繞索使半徑改變，仍用固定換算會累積位置誤差；索在輪槽滑移又可能讓兩個轉速訊號一致但實際行程不同，必須有獨立位移證據。~Multiple layers alter radius and accumulate position error under a fixed conversion. Rope slip can leave rotational signals agreeing while actual travel differs, requiring independent displacement evidence.||減速比增加會在保持轉矩不變下額外創造機械功率。~Increasing gear reduction creates additional mechanical power without changing torque demand.
塔架側移與導向~Tower sway and guidance||高塔的側向柔度改變導向間隙和索具幾何，風與熱作用可能疊加。簡化懸臂模型適合比較剛度敏感性，不能替代含橫梁與基礎的整體模型。~Tower lateral flexibility changes guide clearance and rope geometry, with wind and thermal effects interacting. A cantilever model compares stiffness sensitivity without replacing the full frame and foundation model.||假設等效懸臂高80 m、頂部橫力200 kN、EI=4×10¹² N·m²，δ=FL³/(3EI)=8.533 mm；線彈性單柱近似。~Assume equivalent cantilever height 80 m, top force 200 kN and EI=4×10¹² N·m². δ=FL³/(3EI)=8.533 mm, a linear-elastic single-column approximation.||用塔頂與中段測點重建變形形狀，對照風向、溫度和基礎傾斜；檢查是否符合懸臂曲線，再決定是否需要框架或地基耦合模型。~Reconstruct deflection shape from top and intermediate targets and compare wind, temperature and foundation tilt. Check the cantilever shape before deciding whether frame or soil coupling is required.||基礎轉動能產生近似線性側移，不能全歸因於塔柱彎曲。單點位移也可能受測站移動影響，若缺少獨立基準就會誤判導向系統的幾何變化。~Foundation rotation creates near-linear displacement that should not all be attributed to bending. A moving survey station can also imitate sway and misidentify changes in guidance geometry without independent references.||塔頂偏移只能由塔柱本身彎曲造成，基礎不會影響。~Top displacement can only come from tower bending and is unaffected by foundations.
配重行程與幾何邊界~Counterweight travel and geometric limits||船廂與配重之間的索路幾何決定行程比，不能僅由名稱推定一比一。滑輪組、端部空間與纜索彈伸共同限制可達位置。~Rope routing determines the travel ratio between caisson and counterweight; it cannot be inferred from terminology alone. Pulley arrangements, endpoint space and rope extension jointly constrain reachable positions.||假設理想索路長度約束x+2y=constant，船廂上升60 m則配重位移y=−30 m；此為教學滑輪配置，非宣稱本站索路。~Assume an ideal teaching rope constraint x+2y=constant. A caisson rise of 60 m gives counterweight displacement y=−30 m; this is not a claim about the actual site routing.||沿圖面追蹤每段索長變化，逐一核對固定和活動滑輪；用低速量測的兩端位移比驗算幾何，並把伸長補償和端部餘裕分開。~Trace length change along every rope segment, identifying fixed and moving pulleys. Verify geometry using measured endpoint travel ratios and separate extension compensation from end-clearance allowance.||把虛構滑輪比例套到實際系統會直接錯估行程，索具伸長也會改變端部餘裕。即使中段運動正常，端部空間不足仍可能成為主要限制。~Applying an assumed pulley ratio to the real system misstates travel, while rope extension changes endpoint clearance. Normal mid-travel motion does not establish adequate space near the ends.||任何船廂與配重系統的移動距離都一定相同。~Every caisson-counterweight arrangement necessarily has equal travel distances.
制動動能與停止距離~Braking energy and stopping distance||制動需吸收整個移動系統的動能，配重不會抵銷動能。停止距離與減速度相關，而不平衡重力可能在同一方向持續加入能量。~Brakes absorb kinetic energy of the moving system, which counterweights do not cancel. Stopping distance depends on deceleration, while imbalance gravity may continue adding energy in the direction of motion.||假設等效移動質量16 million kg、速度0.15 m/s，動能mv²/2=180 kJ；若恆減速度0.01 m/s²，停止距離v²/(2a)=1.125 m。~Assume equivalent moving mass 16 million kg and speed 0.15 m/s, giving kinetic energy 180 kJ. Constant deceleration 0.01 m/s² gives stopping distance 1.125 m.||將制動起始位置、速度和停止位置同時核對，積分實測減速度驗算距離；另記錄制動熱與重力方向，區分動能吸收和持續荷載。~Check initial position, velocity and final position together, integrating measured deceleration to verify distance. Record brake heat and gravity direction separately to distinguish kinetic absorption from sustained loading.||反應延遲會在真正減速前增加行程，固定減速度也可能因摩擦溫升而失效。只以低速空載停止測試推論高能量工況，會低估距離與熱負擔。~Response delay adds travel before deceleration, and heating may invalidate constant braking force. Extrapolating a slow unloaded stop to high-energy conditions understates distance and thermal demand on the braking system.||配重平衡後，制動器就不需要吸收系統的動能。~Once counterweights balance gravity the brakes need absorb no kinetic energy.
對接間隙充水體積~Docking-gap filling volume||船廂與固定航道之間的間隙需要形成可控水域，間隙體積影響水位變化和密封負荷。幾何體積不是漏水量，兩者應以不同量測辨認。~The docking gap between caisson and fixed reach forms a controlled water volume. Its geometry influences level change and seal loading, but gap volume is not leakage and requires a separate measurement interpretation.||假設有效對接截面50 m²、間隙長0.25 m，充水體積12.5 m³；若由面積1000 m²船廂供應，理想水位下降12.5 mm。~Assume docking cross-section 50 m² and gap length 0.25 m, giving fill volume 12.5 m³. Supplied by a 1000 m² caisson, ideal level reduction is 12.5 mm.||以間隙幾何、充水累積量與船廂水位三者互核，確認填滿後流量是否回到預期基線；將短時儲水和持續漏流分成不同判讀窗口。~Cross-check gap geometry, cumulative filling and caisson level, verifying flow returns to its expected baseline after filling. Use separate interpretation windows for temporary storage and sustained leakage.||若把正常間隙填水當成密封漏流，會誤判設備狀況；反之持續漏水被短時大流量掩蓋時也可能漏報。水位解析度不足更會使兩種原因難以區分。~Normal gap filling can be mistaken for seal leakage, while large initial flow can conceal sustained leakage. Inadequate level resolution further obscures the distinction between temporary storage and a continuing defect.||對接時量到的全部進水量都一定是止水失效漏流。~All water measured during docking must be leakage caused by seal failure.
雙船廂服務與可用度~Two-caisson service and availability||兩座獨立船廂可以增加服務彈性，但共用航道與維修資源會形成瓶頸。至少一座可用和兩座同時達到全部容量，是不同的可靠度問題。~Two independent caissons improve service flexibility, but shared approaches and maintenance resources can constrain capacity. Availability of at least one differs from simultaneous availability of full two-caisson throughput.||假設兩船廂獨立可用度各0.95，至少一座可用為1−0.05²=0.9975；兩座同時可用0.95²=0.9025，未含共同原因。~Assume independent caisson availability 0.95 each. At least one is available with probability 0.9975, while both are available with probability 0.9025, excluding common causes.||分別統計部分服務和完整容量時段，核對共用供電、航道與排程限制；檢查兩座停機是否在相同事件中發生，再判斷獨立性是否合理。~Count partial-service and full-capacity periods separately, checking shared power, approaches and scheduling. Identify outages occurring in the same event before accepting an independence assumption.||把至少一座可用率當作完整容量可用率會誇大通行能力，共用航道停用又可能讓兩座正常設備都無法服務。必須先定義成功條件再引用數值。~Using at-least-one availability as full-capacity availability exaggerates throughput. A closed shared approach can prevent both healthy caissons from serving traffic, so success must be defined before quoting probabilities.||至少一座船廂可用就代表整個系統完整容量可用。~At least one available caisson means full system capacity is available.
''')
 for i,ex,out,un in [(1,'1000*1200*.03/1000',36,'t'),(2,'64*.2/10',1.28,'MN'),(3,'2*1.2/(.8+1.2)',1.2,'MN'),(4,'4/.08',50,'ratio'),(5,'60*.15/(2*math.pi*1.5)',.95492966,'rpm'),(6,'200e3*80**3/(3*4e12)*1000',8.533333,'mm'),(7,'-60/2',-30,'m'),(8,'16e6*.15**2/2/1000',180,'kJ'),(9,'50*.25/1000*1000',12.5,'mm'),(10,'1-.05**2',.9975,'availability')]:a('b228',i,ex,out,un)
 c('b229','旋轉升船的浮力平衡、齒輪定向與循環能量~Buoyant balance, geared orientation and cycle energy in a rotating boat lift',['sc-wheel','sc-carbon','sc-location'],r'''
成對船槽質量平衡~Paired gondola mass balance||水輪兩端船槽以近似相等總質量降低重力轉矩，浮船排出等重水是關鍵。但船槽水位差、積水和附著物仍會破壞理想對稱。~Paired gondolas reduce gravitational torque by maintaining nearly equal total masses, using equal-weight displacement by floating boats. Level differences, retained water and deposits can still break the ideal symmetry.||取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設每槽面積200 m²、其中一槽水位多0.02 m，淡水質量差4 t；若水平力臂12 m，最大重力轉矩Δmgr=470.88 kN·m。~Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume gondola area 200 m² and one level higher by 0.02 m, giving freshwater imbalance 4 t. At horizontal lever arm 12 m, maximum gravity torque Δmgr=470.88 kN·m.||比較兩槽水位與總重推估，將浮船排水和多餘儲水分開；用正反向轉矩差核對不平衡來源，再檢查最大差值是否出現在水平位置。~Compare both levels and inferred mass, separating vessel displacement from excess stored water. Use opposite-direction torque differences to check imbalance and determine whether its maximum occurs near the horizontal position.||船舶自由浮動不代表船槽水位自動相同，排水路徑受阻時額外水量仍會增加。只看船舶重量而忽略水位，會把真正不平衡原因歸錯對象。~Free flotation does not automatically equalize gondola levels, and obstructed drainage can retain extra water. Looking only at vessel mass while ignoring level misidentifies the source of the gravitational imbalance.||兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。~With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels.
重力轉矩隨角度~Gravity torque versus angle||質量差對旋轉軸的力臂隨角度改變，垂直位置重力轉矩可以接近零，水平位置則較大。固定轉矩模型無法描述整個半圈動作。~The lever arm of a mass imbalance changes with angle. Gravity torque can approach zero vertically and peak horizontally, so constant torque cannot describe an entire half-turn.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設質量差3000 kg、半徑12 m、相對水平角60°，τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m；限集中質量與平面剛體。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume imbalance 3000 kg, radius 12 m and angle sixty degrees above horizontal. τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m, for planar rigid motion with concentrated masses.||將實測轉矩扣除慣性項後對轉角作圖，比較餘弦形狀；再以不同旋轉方向辨別摩擦符號，確認角度零點和重力方向一致。~Plot measured torque minus inertia against angle and compare the cosine shape. Use opposite rotation to distinguish friction sign and verify consistent angle zero and gravity direction.||若把角度從垂直量起卻沿用餘弦公式，轉矩峰值位置會錯九十度。傳動摩擦和風力也可能改變曲線，不能把所有殘差當成質量差。~Using an angle measured from vertical in a horizontal-reference cosine shifts the predicted peak by ninety degrees. Friction and wind also alter the curve, so residuals do not uniquely reveal mass imbalance.||質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。~A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation.
船槽水平與齒輪定向~Gondola leveling by gearing||船槽需要在主輪轉動時保持接近水平，定向機構抵銷支臂相對地面的旋轉。這是運動學約束，不是只靠自由擺動就能保證的結果。~Gondolas remain approximately horizontal by counteracting the arm rotation relative to the ground. This is a kinematic constraint rather than a result guaranteed solely by free swinging.||假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。~Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it. Ground-referenced change is zero, an ideal opposite one-to-one relation rather than actual site tooth counts.||以地面水平基準同時量主臂和船槽角度，檢查兩角和在全行程是否穩定；將齒隙造成的換向偏差和結構撓曲分開繪製。~Measure arm and gondola angles against a ground-level reference and check their sum over the full travel. Plot reversal backlash separately from structural bending instead of combining them into one orientation error.||齒隙會在換向時形成短暫角度誤差，軸承阻力也可能使自由懸吊無法理想跟隨。只在上下終點檢查水平，可能漏掉中途最大的船槽傾斜。~Backlash creates brief reversal errors and bearing resistance prevents ideal free following. Checking level only at upper and lower endpoints can miss the largest gondola tilt during intermediate rotation.||只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。~A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.
旋轉速度與旅程~Rotation speed and travel||半圈旋轉的平均角速度與最大角速度不同，啟停段必須留出加減速。船槽線速度也隨半徑變化，不能把軸的轉速當成乘客的平移速度。~Mean half-turn angular speed differs from maximum speed because start and stop need acceleration. Gondola linear speed also depends on radius, so shaft rotation is not passenger translation speed.||假設半圈轉動歷時300 s、勻速近似，ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s；半徑12 m的速度v=ωr=0.12566 m/s。~Assume a half-turn over 300 s with uniform-speed approximation. ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s and speed at radius 12 m is v=ωr=0.12566 m/s.||從角位置歷線估算速度並核對線性位移，清楚標記加減速段；比較平均值與峰值，並確認資料濾波沒有把短時速度變化抹去。~Estimate speed from angle history and verify it against linear travel, marking acceleration intervals. Compare mean and peak values and ensure filtering has not erased brief changes in speed.||將全程平均速度當成處處相同會低估加速段需求，非均勻運轉亦影響水面晃蕩。若半徑取到錯誤位置，換算船槽邊緣速度也會系統性偏差。~Using average speed everywhere misses acceleration demand, while nonuniform movement excites water sloshing. A radius taken to the wrong point also systematically miscalculates speed at the gondola edge.||半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。~Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant.
轉動慣量與加速~Rotational inertia and acceleration||質量平衡消除部分重力需求，卻不消除轉動慣量。遠離軸心的質量對慣量按半徑平方增加，因此外緣附加設備對啟停需求尤其敏感。~Mass balance removes some gravity demand but not rotational inertia. Mass farther from the axis contributes with radius squared, making equipment added near the rim especially important during starting and stopping.||假設兩槽各250000 kg、集中於半徑12 m，I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²；角加速度0.0002 rad/s²需14.4 kN·m，未含輪臂。~Assume two gondolas each 250000 kg concentrated at radius 12 m. I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²; angular acceleration 0.0002 rad/s² requires 14.4 kN·m, excluding wheel arms.||按實際質量分布建立慣量清單，核對槽、輪臂、傳動與附加設備；以加速段轉矩扣除重力和摩擦後比較，檢查是否遺漏旋轉件。~Create an inertia inventory from actual mass distribution, including gondolas, arms, drivetrain and additions. Compare acceleration torque after subtracting gravity and friction, checking for omitted rotating components.||把全部質量放在單一半徑只是簡化，輪臂分布和傳動反射慣量可能不可忽略。若用靜態平衡證明馬達能力，便完全漏掉啟停時的動力需求。~A single-radius mass representation is approximate; distributed arms and reflected drivetrain inertia may matter. Static balance alone cannot establish motor capability because it omits starting and stopping demand.||兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。~Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero.
整循環能量與損失~Full-cycle energy and losses||理想成對升降可互相交換位能，實際電力主要補足損失和不平衡。整循環比較須包括正負功率與輔助設備，不能用某一瞬間功率乘任意時間。~Ideal paired motion exchanges potential energy, while electricity covers losses and imbalance. A cycle balance includes positive and negative power and auxiliaries rather than multiplying one instantaneous reading by an arbitrary duration.||假設平均主驅動功率18 kW持續300 s，另輔助4 kW持續600 s，總能量=(18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh；非官方耗能。~Assume main drive averages 18 kW for 300 s and auxiliaries 4 kW for 600 s. Total energy is (18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh, not official energy use.||積分完整循環的雙向電功率，清楚標示電表是否包含輔機和待機；比較相同水位、天候與船型條件的循環，避免不同邊界的數值相互排名。~Integrate bidirectional power over a complete cycle and identify auxiliary and standby coverage. Compare cycles at matched levels, weather and vessel conditions rather than ranking values with different energy boundaries.||忽略待機與門控能耗會低估每次服務能源，將回生能量在不同邊界重複扣除也會失真。宣傳用水壺類比缺乏共同容量時，不能替代電表紀錄。~Omitting standby and gate-control loads understates service energy, while subtracting regeneration twice distorts the balance. Kettle analogies without common capacity and duration cannot replace metered energy records.||設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。~Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle.
螺栓預拉與接觸~Bolt pretension and joint contact||輪臂連接的螺栓預拉力保持接觸並影響疲勞應力範圍，外力並非全部直接加到螺栓上。接頭剛度決定螺栓與被夾件的載荷分配。~Pretension maintains contact and affects bolt fatigue range. Applied load does not all go directly into the bolt because relative bolt and clamped-part stiffness controls sharing.||假設單螺栓預拉300 kN、接頭剛度分配係數0.2、外拉力100 kN，未分離時螺栓力320 kN、夾緊力減少80 kN。~Assume bolt pretension 300 kN, stiffness fraction 0.2 and applied tension 100 kN. Before separation bolt force becomes 320 kN and clamping force falls by 80 kN.||用校準方法核對預拉而非只讀扳手扭矩，查接觸面是否分離或滑移；將外載循環造成的螺栓應變幅與剛度分配模型交叉比較。~Verify pretension with a calibrated method rather than torque alone, checking separation and slip. Compare cyclic bolt strain with the predicted stiffness sharing under the applied loading cycle.||表面嵌入和鬆弛可能降低夾緊力而扭矩標記仍在，接頭分離後線性分配失效。若把全部外力忽略或全部加到螺栓，都會誤判疲勞需求。~Embedment and relaxation can reduce clamp force despite intact torque marks, and separation invalidates linear sharing. Either ignoring applied load or adding it entirely to bolts misstates fatigue demand.||預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。~All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt.
管形輪臂局部剛度~Tubular-arm section stiffness||管形截面把材料移到外側提高彎曲剛度，但薄壁局部屈曲和焊接細節仍可能控制。截面慣性矩只描述整體彎曲，不能取代局部板件分析。~Tubular sections place material outward to increase bending stiffness, but local shell buckling and welded details can govern. Section inertia describes overall bending rather than local wall behavior.||假設圓管外徑1 m、內徑0.9 m，I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴；均勻完整圓管，不含開孔和局部薄化。~Assume circular tube outer diameter 1 m and inner diameter 0.9 m. I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴, for an intact uniform tube without openings or local thinning.||核對截面幾何與測厚分布，將開孔、加勁和焊縫位置納入模型；用多點應變檢查線性彎曲分布是否足夠，另查局部凹陷。~Check geometry and thickness distribution, including openings, stiffeners and weld locations. Use multiple strains to test linear bending assumptions and inspect local dents separately from overall member curvature.||局部凹陷可能觸發薄壁失穩，即使全截面慣性矩幾乎不變。平均厚度無法代表腐蝕坑或焊趾附近的局部承載，不能只以整體撓度驗收。~A local dent can trigger shell instability with little change in overall inertia. Mean thickness misses pits and local weld-toe demands, so global deflection alone cannot establish local adequacy.||管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。~Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling.
水面晃蕩時間尺度~Free-surface sloshing time scale||船槽加速度會激起自由液面晃蕩，運動頻率與水深、槽長共同決定反應。小振幅理論可比較尺度，實際船體和隔板會改變流場。~Gondola acceleration excites free-surface sloshing whose response depends on motion frequency, water depth and tank length. Small-amplitude theory compares scales, while vessels and baffles modify the real flow.||取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設矩形槽長20 m、水深2 m，k=π/L，ω²=gk tanh(kh)，第一模態T=2π/ω=9.177 s；無船且小振幅。~Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume rectangular tank length 20 m and depth 2 m, with k=π/L and ω²=gk tanh(kh). First-mode T=2π/ω=9.177 s, for small motion without a vessel.||比較槽內不同位置水位相位與船槽加速度頻譜，辨認駐波節點；用有船和無船資料分開驗證，並保留感測器飽和或濺水段。~Compare level phase at several positions with gondola-acceleration spectra and identify standing-wave nodes. Validate occupied and empty conditions separately, preserving sensor saturation and splash intervals in the record.||船體遮擋會分割水面並改變模態，大幅晃蕩與撞壁亦超出線性理論。若只取槽中央測站，可能恰好位於節點而錯認沒有晃蕩。~A hull subdivides the free surface and changes modes, while large sloshing and wall impact exceed linear theory. A central sensor may sit near a node and falsely suggest no motion.||只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。~A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response.
運河高差與分段提升~Canal elevation and staged lifting||整個運河連接高差可以由水輪與其他船閘共同完成，不能把整體高差全歸給單一設備。分段能量與水量盤點需要明確界定每個控制體。~A canal-level difference can be shared between a wheel and additional locks. Assigning the entire difference to one device misstates geometry; staged energy and water accounting requires clear control boundaries.||假設全線高差35 m、水輪部分24 m，其他設施需補11 m；這是分段算例，僅35 m採官方運河背景，24 m為教學假設。~Assume total route difference 35 m and wheel portion 24 m, leaving 11 m for other facilities. Only 35 m is official canal context; 24 m is a teaching assumption.||沿完整航路建立同基準縱剖面，逐一標出水輪、船閘與渠道水面；檢查宣傳高度、結構高度和實際提升高度的定義，避免相互替代。~Build a common-datum profile along the complete route, marking wheel, locks and reach levels. Check definitions of advertised height, structural height and actual lift before using them interchangeably.||把景觀總高度當提升高度會誇大能量需求，漏掉上游船閘又會低估通行時間與用水。即使單一設備運轉正常，全航路仍可能受到其他節點限制。~Using overall architectural height as lift exaggerates energy demand, while omitting upper locks understates transit time and water use. A functioning wheel does not establish availability of the whole route.||官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。~The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone.
''')
 for i,ex,out,un in [(1,'200*.02*1000*9.81*12/1000',470.88,'kN m'),(2,'3000*9.81*12*.5/1000',176.58,'kN m'),(3,'180-180',0,'degree'),(4,'math.pi/300*12',.12566371,'m/s'),(5,'2*250000*12**2*.0002/1000',14.4,'kN m'),(6,'(18*300+4*600)/3600',2.1666667,'kWh'),(7,'300+.2*100',320,'kN'),(8,'math.pi*(1-.9**4)/64',.01688115,'m4'),(9,'2*math.pi/math.sqrt(9.81*(math.pi/20)*math.tanh(math.pi/20*2))',9.1768633,'s'),(10,'35-24',11,'m')]:a('b229',i,ex,out,un)
